          "resource_manifest": "third_party/statechart-provenance.json",
          "adaptations": [
            "Align the existing workflow texts with the 0.15.43 simplifications while retaining the single domain router and nanobot-native helpers.",
            "Remove retired how, why, architect, and reflect prompt/reference trees; route large or cross-cutting work through figure-it-out instead of the removed Orchestrate playbook.",
            "Keep how direct by default rather than requiring one subagent; retain bounded inherited-model delegation and no-subagent restrictions.",
            "Propagate worker.md by absolute path, without adopting unconditional external-action authority, extra acceptance gates, or a prohibition on necessary user decisions.",
            "Preserve exact-snapshot proof, repository acceptance requirements, scoped resource ownership, protected profiles/memory, and immutable installed packages.",
            "Keep plans in the conversation unless persistence is requested; experiments, publication, history changes, and landing remain authorization-bound.",
            "Retain semantic and authorization checks at mutable boundaries, bounded measurements, useful regression coverage, and source uncertainty in the shorter principles and writing methods.",
            "Add on-demand Statechart and formal-verifier creation/maintenance, preserving source-to-model correspondence, bounded claims, mutation sensitivity, and counterexample replay rather than making formal checking a mandatory gate.",
            "Retain the Statechart semantic engine and regression corpus; adapt explicit external dependencies, CRLF input, Windows/POSIX process ownership, timeout/cancellation, and immutable-package output boundaries. Record per-file changes in resource_manifest."
          ],
          "excluded_updates": [
            "Cursor-specific model slugs, reasoning budgets, agents, and the generated Claude Code adapter.",
            "Upstream forge watchers and plan-checker deletion: those executable helpers were not part of this nanobot port."
          ]
        }
